{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b6ee-434b-74f6-ab26-96b3f0b01551","session_id":"01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_sN9t6xkCGQQ7HDIWCczb7168","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully created and wrote to new file: C:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\.collab\\worktrees\\004\\lib\\contract\\validate.mjs"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","_messageId":"01a1b6ee1bbb7097b622117aae991cc2","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6ee1bbb7097b622117aae991cc2","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6ee1bbb7097b622117aae991cc2","traceparent":"00-e2db99401a709910f956cc03bd750ebc-3271128b70b8e57d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:53:50.543Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6ee-4357-7f9e-be6c-785f0bf8c972","session_id":"01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd","message":{"id":"01a1b6ee43577f9ebe6c785d5fb4ed92","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Issue: `type` check: for integer type, typeOf returns 'integer' for integers so number type check on integer passes since matchesType('number') typeof number true. Fine.\n\nCareful: type check early-return means if type fails, other keywords skipped. Good (avoid cascade).\n\nNow views.mjs and scan.mjs.\n\nviews.mjs:\n```js\nexport const VIEW_NAMES = ['agentline','full','draft']\nexport function resolveView({transport, request, hasSession}) {...}\n```\nCareful: VIEW_NAMES exported; purity test checks no node: imports and no Date.now etc.\n\ndraft = request.schema === undefined || request.compat === 'draft'. Note if request has schema undefined but compat 'x' → draft true. Yes.\n\ncli full → error E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN.\n\nNow scan.mjs.\n\nRules:\n- iterative stack traversal.\n- object keys lowercased exact match in forbidden.keys.\n- values: each string value and each object key, lowercase, whole-word match against forbidden values set (catalog ids, keys, executable names).\n- whole-word boundary chars are [a-z0-9] (after lowercase).\n- skip call subtrees for key/value scanning; compare template instead.\n\nCall subtree detection: key named 'call' anywhere? Design: \"键名为 `call` 的值，以及顶层数组 `calls` 的每个元素，视为 call 子树\". So when traversing, if a key (any case? presumably exact 'call') whose value is object → treat as call. And top-level `calls` array elements.\n\nPath: JSON pointer. For `models[i].call` path is `/models/0/call`. Hits for call_mismatch path points to error location.\n\nTemplate args: `[wrapper.bin,\"run\",\"--lease\",<lease>,\"--state-dir\",wrapper.state_dir,\"--config\",wrapper.config]`.\n- `<lease>`: from sibling handle's lease_id. For models[i].call → models[i].lease_id. For calls[i] → models[i].lease_id (same index).\n- If no sibling lease: require args[3] matches ^l_[A-Za-z0-9]+$.\n\nImplementation: walk with stack of {value, path, parent...}. Need to know context for call: pass `lease` when pushing.\n\nPlan: traversal frames {node, pointer, lease}. Where lease is set when descending into `models[i].call`.\n\nWe need, when at root object, handle:\n- for each key k:\n  - if k === 'call' and value is object → validateCall(value, pointer/k, leaseFromSibling?) — lease from the containing object if it has lease_id.\n  - else generic scan.\n- if k === 'calls' and Array → each element treated as call with lease = models[index]?.lease_id (root-level models).\n\nSimplest: traversal from root with node + pointer + parentLease (the lease_id of the enclosing object) and a flag `isRoot`. When encountering key 'call': push frame {kind:'call', value, pointer, lease: node.lease_id ?? null}. When encountering key 'calls' at root: for each element push {kind:'call', value: element, pointer: `${pointer}/${i}`, lease: root.models?.[i]?.lease_id ?? null}.\n\nHmm careful for handle-full: call is under top-level object? handle-full has `call` and `lease_id` at same level. Good.\n\nNested `call` deeper (e.g., inside detail)? \"键名为 call 的值\" — any. Use node.lease_id if present else inherited? Use node.lease_id ?? outer lease maybe. I'll use node.lease_id if string else inherited lease.\n\nGeneric scan for objects: for each key:\n- key check: lowercase key in forbiddenKeys → hit {path: pointer/key, kind:'forbidden_key'}.\n- value check if string: scan string.\n- key value check: \"每个对象键，转小写后对禁用值集合做整词匹配\" — keys also scanned as values. So check key string against forbidden values → hit at path pointer/key with kind forbidden_value. Careful: \"同一路径同一禁用值只报一次\" — key hit path same as key hit; if key is both forbidden_key and forbidden_value (unlikely), both reported with different kinds. Fine.\n\nFor arrays: elements at index paths; strings scanned.\n\nDepth: explicit stack, so deep nesting safe.\n\nValue scanning: for forbidden value `v`, find occurrences: indexOf loop; check char before and after not in [a-z0-9]. Lowercase both. For each distinct matched value per path, only one hit.\n\nCareful: \"非字符串值（数字、布尔、null）不扫\".\n\ncall validation errors: `call_mismatch` with path to error and match field name:\n- keys mismatch → path = call pointer, match 'keys'\n- command !== wrapper.command → path = `${p}/command`, match 'command'\n- input !== 'stdin' → `/input`\n- output !== 'cliworker.event/v1' → `/output`\n- cwd not string → `/cwd` match 'cwd'\n- timeout_ms not integer >=1 → `/timeout_ms`\n- args length !== 8 → `/args` match 'args'\n- args[i] mismatch → `/args/${i}` match `args[i]` (design example says `args[3]`). Hmm: \"match 为字段名如 `command`、`args[3]`、`keys`\". So for args element use `args[3]` string, and path `/args/3`. OK.\n\nShould we report multiple errors per call? E-3 expects `[...new Set(bad.hits.map(h=>h.kind))].join()` === 'call_mismatch' — only kinds. Count not checked there. Test 33 expects \"各一个 call_mismatch\" for each of 4 mutations: change command → 1; change args[3] → presumably 1; missing key → 1; extra key → 1. So per mutation we must produce exactly 1 hit. For args[3] change: only args[3] mismatch → 1. For missing key: keys mismatch → report and stop (don't also report args length or other fields). For extra key: same.\n\nSo: if keys mismatch → single hit and return. Otherwise check each field; to be safe also stop after first mismatch? Test only expects 1 for command change (command mismatch only). Multiple fields could match if e.g. command changed → args[0] might still equal wrapper.bin, so only 1. But if command changed to something and args[0] differ too... in test they change only command. I'll report all mismatches but short-circuit keys. Hmm, design says \"不符报 call_mismatch ... 逐项比较模板\". Multiple is fine. But for extra key `model`, keys mismatch → stop. Good.\n\nAlso, when E-3's `bad` has same call in models[0].call and calls[0]: `v(call({command:'zetacli'}))` returns {models:[{lease_id,call}], calls:[c]}. So two call subtrees both mismatch → 2 hits, kinds dedupe to call_mismatch. Fine.\n\nWait, but in E-3 `ok` case: calls[0] lease from models[0].lease_id. Good.\n\nAlso note: call subtree skip means the `call` key itself should not trigger forbidden_key (call not in forbidden keys anyway). And `env_names` inside detail.direct_call gets scanned normally (it's in forbidden keys) — direct_call itself is forbidden key. Fine.\n\nOne more: `call` value must be compared even when nested inside `direct_call`? direct_call has its own shape (command,args,cwd,input,env_names) but it's under key direct_call, not call. Only key exactly 'call'.\n\nNow `catalog` shape {models:[{key,id,cli}]}. Executable name: take path last segment, strip extension (.exe/.cmd/.bat/.ps1/.mjs), lowercase. cli may be path with / or \\.\n\nForbidden values set includes full `cli` string? Design: \"禁用值集合 = catalog 中全部 id、key 与可执行名\". So not the whole path, just executable name. But `key` may contain ':' e.g. `claude:claude-sonnet-5-5` — whole word match: boundary chars [a-z0-9], ':' is not alnum, so ok.\n\nTest E-2: catalog {key:'k:zeta-model-9', id:'zeta-model-9', cli:'zetacli'}; value 'use zeta-model-9 now' → hits forbidden_value at /a/0/m. Note key 'k:zeta-model-9' isn't in text. Good.\n\nBut careful: scanning `{note:'cliworker config dsh-CLIWorker'}` — catalog values are zeta stuff, so no hits. Test 32 uses catalog with claude etc.\n\nNow boundary check: forbidden value may start with non-alnum (rare). Implement:\n\n```js\nfunction wholeWord(hay, needle) {\n  let from = 0\n  while (true) {\n    const idx = hay.indexOf(needle, from)\n    if (idx === -1) return false\n    const before = idx === 0 ? '' : hay[idx-1]\n    const after = hay[idx+needle.length] ?? ''\n    if (!isAlnum(before) && !isAlnum(after)) return true\n    from = idx + 1\n  }\n}\n```\nisAlnum('') → false.\n\nAlso dedupe by path+value.\n\nNow let me write scan.mjs.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","_messageId":"01a1b6ee43577f9ebe6c785d5fb4ed92","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6ee43577f9ebe6c785d5fb4ed92","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6ee43577f9ebe6c785d5fb4ed92","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6ee-4357-7f9e-be6c-785f0bf8c972","traceparent":"00-e2db99401a709910f956cc03bd750ebc-3271128b70b8e57d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:54:12.578Z"}
