{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b6ee-9976-7c77-9c99-0c970e81e3f1","session_id":"01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_zg6nSUyoEfeSZkUheKuT0383","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully created and wrote to new file: C:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\.collab\\worktrees\\004\\lib\\contract\\scan.mjs"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","_messageId":"01a1b6ee43577f9ebe6c785d5fb4ed92","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6ee43577f9ebe6c785d5fb4ed92","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6ee43577f9ebe6c785d5fb4ed92","traceparent":"00-e2db99401a709910f956cc03bd750ebc-3271128b70b8e57d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:54:12.600Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6ee-9980-7fb3-82ea-b47523ec55ce","session_id":"01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd","message":{"id":"01a1b6ee997f73e5874539c25b3a9177","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bug: the stack pops frames LIFO, and I use a separate recursive-ish structure; fine. But for `calls` handling I check `pointer === ''` only at root. `frame.fromRoot` undefined—simplify: only root-level `calls`. Design says \"顶层数组 `calls`\". So condition `pointer === ''` suffices. Remove fromRoot.\n\nAlso array scanning pushes objects; but object frame that is an array element could contain key 'calls' — pointer non-empty so ignored. fine.\n\nAnother issue: `scanString(String(key), path)` — the key itself scanned as value; for forbidden key case this may also add a forbidden_value hit at same path. Only if key is also a catalog value.\n\nAlso: dedupe of forbidden_key? If same path... unique anyway.\n\nCritical: `hits` order. E-2 expects `[[\"/a/0/m\",\"forbidden_value\"]]` — only one hit. Fine.\n\nE-1 expects `[[\"/a/b/Model_Key\",\"forbidden_key\"]]`. With my code: key 'Model_Key' → forbidden_key hit at /a/b/Model_Key. Then scanString('model_key') against catalog values (zeta-model-9, k:zeta-model-9, zetacli) → none. Good.\n\nE-3: ok case yields 0 hits: call keys exactly, command 'node' equals wrapper.command 'node', args[0]='bin/cliworker.mjs' equals wrapper.bin, args[3] 'l_abc' equals lease 'l_abc' from models[0].lease_id, args[5] '/s' equals state_dir, args[7] '/c' equals config, cwd string contains model id but no scan → 0. \n\nBut careful: models[0] has keys lease_id and call. The `models` array is traversed; model object: key 'lease_id' scanned as string value 'l_abc' — no forbidden match. key 'call' → checkCall. Then `calls` at root → checkCall again. Good.\n\nbad case: command 'zetacli'. checkCall reports command mismatch only (args[0] still bin). 2 hits both call_mismatch. ok.\n\nPotential problem: `wrapper.command` For calls, design says `command === wrapper.command`. In test 33 they use wrapper with command maybe 'node'. Good.\n\nAlso in E-2/E-3 wrapper passed as `w={command:'node',bin:...}` — yes.\n\nNow remove `frame.fromRoot`.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","_messageId":"01a1b6ee997f73e5874539c25b3a9177","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6ee997f73e5874539c25b3a9177","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6ee997f73e5874539c25b3a9177","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6ee-9980-7fb3-82ea-b47523ec55ce","traceparent":"00-e2db99401a709910f956cc03bd750ebc-3271128b70b8e57d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:54:18.293Z"}
