{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6f1-7ec0-7afa-9388-817325a1094c","session_id":"01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd","message":{"id":"01a1b6f17ec07afa93888171f39bbe47","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue: when validating selection-ok.v1, a nested `$ref` to \"handle.v1.schema.json#/$defs/call\" then the resolved handle schema's internal `\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/call\"` resolves against the *root* schema (selection-ok) rather than the file it came from. Need to track the current document root for `#` refs.\n\nFix: pass a `rootSchema` context down: validateValue(node, value, pointer, depth, currentRoot). When resolving a file ref, the target becomes the new currentRoot. Local `#/$defs/...` resolves against currentRoot.\n\nLet me refactor resolveRef(ref, currentRoot, loadSchema) returning {schema, root}.\n\nIn validateValue: if $ref: \n```\nconst resolved = resolveRef(node.$ref, rootSchema, loadSchema)\nvalidateValue(resolved.schema, value, pointer, depth+1, resolved.root)\n```\nwhere rootSchema is parameter.\n\nresolveRef:\n- if filePart === '' → target = rootSchema, root = currentRoot.\n- else target = loadSchema(filePart), root = target.\n\nThen validateValue(target, ..., root).\n\nLet me implement.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","_messageId":"01a1b6f17ec07afa93888171f39bbe47","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6f17ec07afa93888171f39bbe47","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6f17ec07afa93888171f39bbe47","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6f1-7ec0-7afa-9388-817325a1094c","traceparent":"00-e2db99401a709910f956cc03bd750ebc-3271128b70b8e57d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:57:27.360Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6f1-923f-7378-8b29-1da7df1501f5","session_id":"01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd","message":{"id":"01a1b6f17ec07afa93888171f39bbe47","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_00_kGAimjoSy8vsc4cSEg5q0347","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"C:\\git\\dsh-CLIWorker\\.collab\\worktrees\\004\\lib\\contract\\validate.mjs","new_string":"function resolveRef(ref, currentRoot, loadSchema) {\n  if (typeof ref !== 'string') throw new TypeError(`$ref must be a string`)\n  const hash = ref.indexOf('#')\n  const filePart = hash === -1 ? ref : ref.slice(0, hash)\n  const pointerPart = hash === -1 ? '' : ref.slice(hash + 1)\n  let target = currentRoot\n  if (filePart !== '') {\n    if (typeof loadSchema !== 'function') throw new TypeError(`cannot resolve $ref without loadSchema: ${ref}`)\n    target = loadSchema(filePart)\n    if (!target || typeof target !== 'object') throw new TypeError(`cannot resolve $ref: ${ref}`)\n  }\n  if (pointerPart === '') return { schema: target, root: target }\n  const match = /^\\/\\$defs\\/([^/]+)$/.exec(pointerPart)\n  if (!match) throw new TypeError(`unsupported $ref: ${ref}`)\n  const name = decodeURIComponent(match[1]).replace(/~1/g, '/').replace(/~0/g, '~')\n  const defs = target.$defs\n  if (!defs || !Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(defs, name)) {\n    throw new TypeError(`cannot resolve $ref: ${ref}`)\n  }\n  return { schema: defs[name], root: target }\n}","old_string":"function resolveRef(ref, rootSchema, loadSchema) {\n  if (typeof ref !== 'string') throw new TypeError(`$ref must be a string`)\n  const hash = ref.indexOf('#')\n  const filePart = hash === -1 ? ref : ref.slice(0, hash)\n  const pointerPart = hash === -1 ? '' : ref.slice(hash + 1)\n  let target = rootSchema\n  if (filePart !== '') {\n    if (typeof loadSchema !== 'function') throw new TypeError(`cannot resolve $ref without loadSchema: ${ref}`)\n    target = loadSchema(filePart)\n    if (!target || typeof target !== 'object') throw new TypeError(`cannot resolve $ref: ${ref}`)\n  }\n  if (pointerPart === '') return target\n  const match = /^\\/\\$defs\\/([^/]+)$/.exec(pointerPart)\n  if (!match) throw new TypeError(`unsupported $ref: ${ref}`)\n  const name = decodeURIComponent(match[1]).replace(/~1/g, '/').replace(/~0/g, '~')\n  const defs = target.$defs\n  if (!defs || !Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(defs, name)) {\n    throw new TypeError(`cannot resolve $ref: ${ref}`)\n  }\n  return defs[name]\n}"}}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":139447,"output_tokens":935,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":138880,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","_messageId":"01a1b6f17ec07afa93888171f39bbe47","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6f17ec07afa93888171f39bbe47","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6f17ec07afa93888171f39bbe47","traceparent":"00-e2db99401a709910f956cc03bd750ebc-3271128b70b8e57d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:57:27.360Z"}
