{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6f1-de29-766a-9783-b1b5514b3c68","session_id":"01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd","message":{"id":"01a1b6f1de29766a9783b1b3e90b9156","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now golden files. Let me compute values carefully.\n\n#### quota-shapes.json (9 cases)\nCases:\n- q-pct-5: quota {remaining_pct:5}, samples [], usage Normal → expected {remaining_fraction:0.05, remaining_mtok:null, risk:\"low_reserve\", risk_basis:\"fraction\"}\n- q-pct-4: {remaining_pct:4} → 0.04, critical, fraction\n- q-pct-0 → 0, exhausted, fraction\n- q-pct-15 → 0.15, ok, fraction\n- q-credits-no-rate: {remaining:1, unit:\"credits\"} → risk unknown, risk_basis none, reason credits_conversion_missing\n- q-credits-zero: {remaining:0, unit:\"credits\"} → risk exhausted\n- q-credits-rate: {remaining:1, unit:\"credits\", credits_per_mtok:1000}, samples 3×{mtok:0.2,cost_usd:null} → remaining_mtok 0.001, tasks_left 0, tasks_left_basis tasks, risk exhausted, risk_basis tasks\n- q-tokens: {remaining:2000000, unit:\"tokens\"} → remaining_mtok 2\n- q-usd: {remaining_usd:3}, samples 3×{mtok:null,cost_usd:0.5} → tasks_left 6, tasks_left_basis usd, risk ok, risk_basis usd\n\n#### b44.json (9 cases)\ninput: {now:\"2026-11-07T10:00:00Z\", reading_ttl_s:600, models, pools, rows}\nmodels: presumably [\"claude:claude-opus-5-5\",\"claude:claude-sonnet-5-5\"] by default.\npools: 5h pool with capacity per model.\nrows: {model, tokens, at}.\n\nexpected: {\"<model key>\": {status, remaining_mtok, reason}}.\n\nComputed earlier:\n1. b44-used-0: reading null, rows [] → O 2, S 10, known, reason null.\n2. b44-reading-half: reading {value:0.5, at 09:55} → O 1, S 5.\n3. b44-ledger-sonnet-1m: reading null, rows S 1e6 @08:00 → O 1.8, S 9.\n   O: 2 - 1e6/(2e6)*... wait formula: used = sum over rows tokens_i/(cap_p(model_i)*1e6). For O cap 2 → 1e6/(2e6)=0.5 → O remaining = 2*(1-0.5)=1? Hmm expected O 1.8.\n\nLet me recompute. Design says b44-ledger-sonnet-1m expected O 1.8, S 9. Hmm: O 1.8 means used 0.1 → 1e6/(10e6)? That doesn't match opus cap 2.\n\nWait: used_p is a fraction of the pool, computed as sum tokens_i/(cap_p(model_i)*1e6) where cap_p(model_i) is the capacity of that model in that pool. For sonnet, cap 10 → 1e6/(10e6) = 0.1 → fraction used 0.1 → remaining S = 10*(0.9)=9 ✓. And O: same pool fraction 0.1 applies to all models in the pool: O remaining = 2*(1-0.1)=1.8 ✓. \n\nSo used fraction is pool-level (not per model), then remaining per model = cap_p(model)*(1-used). Good.\n\n4. b44-reading-then-1m: reading 0.5 @09:55, row S 1e6 @09:58 (after reading). used = 0.5 + 1e6/(10e6)=0.6 → O 2*0.4=0.8, S 10*0.4=4 ✓.\n5. b44-fresh-reading-ignores-earlier-rows: reading 0.5 @09:55, row @08:00 (before reading) → used 0.5 → O 1, S 5 ✓.\n6. b44-stale-reading-uses-ledger: reading 0.5 @09:00 (age 3600 > 600) → ignored; ledger window rows: S 1e6 @08:00, window start 07:00 → used 0.1 → O 1.8, S 9 ✓.\n   reason? maybe reading_stale reason for both? Design expected table: \"O 1.8；S 9\", reason not listed → null. Hmm but reason_stale? It says `reason` 未列则为 null. So reason null. OK.\n7. b44-unknown-capacity-row: row model codex:gpt-x 1000 @08:00, cap unknown → O and S status unknown, remaining_mtok null, reason ledger_capacity_unknown.\n8. b44-rounding: reading {0.33333,09:55} → O = 2*(1-0.33333)=1.33334 → 1.333; S = 10*0.66667=6.6667 → 6.667 ✓.\n9. b44-two-pools-min: models only sonnet; two pools → S 5.\n\nFor case 9, input overrides models and pools.\n\nNote case 7: models presumably [\"claude:claude-opus-5-5\",\"claude:claude-sonnet-5-5\"] and rows with codex model. Expected status unknown for both with reason ledger_capacity_unknown.\n\n#### forecast/thresholds.json 21 cases per table.\n\n#### quantiles 15.\nn12 samples 1..12: sorted [1..12]; Heavy p90: ceil(0.9*12)=ceil(10.8)=11 → sorted[10]=11 ✓. Normal p50: ceil(6)=6 → sorted[5]=6 ✓. Light p25: ceil(3)=3 → sorted[2]=3 ✓.\nn20: Heavy ceil(18)=18 → sorted[17]=18 ✓. Normal 10 → 10 ✓. Light ceil(5)=5 → 5 ✓.\nn3: Heavy ceil(2.7)=3 → 0.3 ✓; Normal ceil(1.5)=2 → 0.2 ✓; Light ceil(0.75)=1 → 0.1 ✓.\nn4 [0.4,0.1,0.3,0.2] sorted [0.1,0.2,0.3,0.4]: Heavy ceil(3.6)=4 → 0.4 ✓; Normal ceil(2)=2 → 0.2 ✓; Light ceil(1)=1 → 0.1 ✓.\n\n#### confidence 11 cases per table.\n\n#### burn-eta 14 cases.\n\nburn: burn = used / max(hours, 1/60).\n- burn-5.5-over-5h: 5.5/5 = 1.1 ✓\n- burn-clamp-zero-hours: 0.3/max(0,1/60)=0.3/(1/60)=18 ✓\n- burn-clamp-tiny-hours: 1/max(0.001,0.016667)=1/0.0166667=60 ✓\n- burn-rounding: 2/3=0.6667→0.667 ✓\n- burn-zero-used: 0/4=0 → 0 ✓\neta: now 10:00, remaining 5, burn 2 → 12:30; reset 12:00 → exhausts false ✓.\neta-before-reset: remaining 1, burn 2 → 10:30 < 12:00 → true ✓.\neta-equal-reset: remaining 1, burn 0.5 → +2h → 12:00 equals reset → `eta < reset_at` false ✓.\neta-empty: remaining 0 → eta 10:00 < 12:00 → true ✓.\nround3 cases ✓.\n\n#### capacity 5 cases.\ncap-k2-low: readings 08:00 0, 09:00 0.25, 10:00 0.5. pairs: (08-09) Δ=0.25, tokens rows in (08:00,09:00] = 08:30 1e6 → 1e6. (09-10) Δ=0.25, rows in (09,10]=09:30 1e6. sum tokens 2e6 / sum Δ 0.5 /1e6 = 4 ✓ k2 low.\ncap-k3-medium: readings 07 0, 08 .125, 09 .25, 10 .375. Δ each .125. tokens: 07:30 1e6 in (07,08]; 08:30 0.5e6 in (08,09]; 09:30 1.5e6 in (09,10]. sum 3e6 / 0.375 /1e6 = 8 ✓ k3 medium.\ncap-k10-high: 11 readings 00:00..10:00, fraction i*0.03125. Δ=0.03125 each, 10 pairs. rows 10 × 250000 in (i, i+1] windows. sum 2.5e6 / (10*0.03125=0.3125) /1e6 = 8 ✓ k10 high.\ncap-discard-small-delta: 08 0.5, 09 0.5078125 (Δ=0.0078125 <0.01 discard), 10 0.7578125 (Δ=0.25). rows 08:30 100000 (in discarded pair), 09:30 2e6 → 2e6/0.25/1e6 = 8 ✓ k1 low.\ncap-reset-pair-ignored: 08 .5, 09 .0625 (Δ negative), 10 .3125 (Δ .25). rows 09:30 2e6 → 8, k1 low ✓.\n\n#### policy 4 files.\ninput: {est_mtok:1, count, importance:'high', policy:{unknown_policy, reserve_fraction_for_high:0.15}, reserve_mtok:0, pools, candidates}.\nNote reserve: avail_p = remaining_p - effective reserve - (importance normal ? ...). For high