{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6f3-aff4-781c-9296-69d5819dd03d","session_id":"01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd","message":{"id":"01a1b6f3aff4781c929669d3df60700a","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Problem: `skipFixture` logic - default mode must skip fixtures only when scanning the real repo. But F-11 runs `--root test/fixtures/no-collab/violating`; root != REPO_ROOT → skipFixture false → but the fixture files are at paths like `lib/a.mjs` relative to that root, not `test/fixtures/no-collab/...`, so the prefix filter wouldn't matter. Good.\n\nBut H: the real repo scan must skip `test/fixtures/no-collab/`. With root == REPO_ROOT, skip. However tests will spawn `--root <repo>` explicitly maybe: test 46 runs on real repo root via `--root ROOT` → path.resolve(root) === REPO_ROOT as long as same path (case?). On Windows, REPO_ROOT derived from script location; ROOT from test computed similarly. Both absolute; string equal. But case differences possible; both from same path chain. Use case-insensitive compare on win32 for safety.\n\nActually simpler and more robust: always skip `test/fixtures/no-collab/` prefixed files, since those are fixtures for this very check. But the design says \"默认模式额外跳过...\" implying --root for fixtures behaves as the scanning root, where files aren't under that prefix anyway. So always skipping that prefix is equivalent and simpler. I'll change to always filter.\n\nAlso fixture `test/fixtures/no-collab/clean` files would otherwise be scanned; they contain no needle so only counts change. Not counted in F-12 because root is the clean dir.\n\nLet me simplify: always filter FIXTURE_PREFIX.\n\nAlso potential issue: `walk` skips node_modules/.git by name only, fine.\n\nAnother: `docs` may not exist currently; we'll create docs/contract.md.\n\nNow the fixtures.\n\nviolating/lib/a.mjs line 1 contains the needle in an import path. Need the file to be a valid-ish mjs? Not executed. Content:\nline1: `import x from '../../.collab/blueprint/x.mjs'` — but the needle must be \".collab\". Using `'.collab/blueprint/x.mjs'` contains it.\n\nBut writing these files with Write tool content containing \".collab\" is fine (only the scanner's own source must build it). Design says \"夹具生成代码\" must concatenate — the test code that generates fixtures, not the fixture files themselves (they must contain the literal).\n\nviolating/scripts/b.mjs line 2 comment with `.collab/tasks/x.json`:\nline1: `// fixture`\nline2: `// see .collab/tasks/001/design.md`\n\nviolating/test/c.txt line1: `refer to .collab/tasks/004/brief.md`\n\nviolating/contracts/d.json: line2 string value contains. So:\nline1: `{`\nline2: `  \"note\": \".collab/blueprint/interfaces.md\",`\nline3: `  \"ok\": true`\nline4: `}`\nHit line 2 ✓.\n\nviolating/docs/e.md line3 all caps `.COLLAB`:\nline1: `# fixture`\nline2: ``\nline3: `Path .COLLAB/blueprint is forbidden here.`\n\nviolating/package.json line2 field value:\nline1 `{`\nline2 `  \"description\": \"contains .collab reference\",`\nline3 `  \"name\": \"fixture\"`\nline4 `}`\n\nclean/lib/a.mjs: no needle. e.g. `export const ok = true`\nclean/package.json: `{ \"name\": \"clean-fixture\" }`.\n\nCareful: F-11 expects exactly 6 FAIL lines with those paths/line numbers. My scanner lists files sorted; each hit. Note contracts/d.json also has other lines without needle. Only line2. ✓\n\nAlso `clean/package.json` counts as 1 file, `clean/lib/a.mjs` 1 → 2 ✓.\n\nNow gen-contract-doc.mjs.\n\nrenderContractDoc(root) → string. Structure:\n\n```\n# CLIWorker 契约（自动生成）\n> 本文件由 scripts/gen-contract-doc.mjs 生成，请勿手改。snapshot_version: 1\n\n## 1. 错误码\n\n| code | exit | http_status | retryable | trigger_id | trigger |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ... |\n\n退出码 0 表示成功（含 truncated），不是错误码，不进入本表。\n\n## 2. 403 触发与判定顺序\n\n| code | trigger_id |\n...\n写路由判定顺序：session > readonly > csrf > body（`write_route_order`）。\n\n## 3. 警告码\n\n- W_FIELD_IGNORED\n...\n\n## 4. 拒选原因\n\n### v1\n...\n### admin_only\n...\n### draft\n...\n\n## 5. draft 到 v1 的原因映射\n\n| draft | v1 |\n\n## 6. forecast 枚举与阈值\n\n...\n### 阈值表 tasks\n...\n```\n\nF-15 only checks lines starting with `#` or `##`. So `###` is fine (not matched). Good — I can use ### subheads.\n\nBut careful: F-15 regex `/^#{1,2} /` matches \"# \" and \"## \" only, so ### ignored. \n\nContent:\n- §9 manifest table path | sha256.\n- §10 schema file names sorted.\n\nMust not include timestamps/absolute paths.\n\ncheck-contract-doc: import renderContractDoc from gen script; compare.\n\ngen script write when invoked directly: `gen-contract-doc: wrote docs/contract.md (<N> bytes)` where N = byte length? Buffer.byteLength of the content.\n\nLet me write.\n\nNote: renderContractDoc(root) root relative resolved against cwd.\n\nAlso the doc must escape `|` in table cells (trigger text may contain none; but `|` possible? e.g. \"full or draft\" no). Implement escape anyway.\n\nNow write gen-contract-doc.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","_messageId":"01a1b6f3aff4781c929669d3df60700a","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6f3aff4781c929669d3df60700a","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6f3aff4781c929669d3df60700a","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6f3-aff4-781c-9296-69d5819dd03d","traceparent":"00-e2db99401a709910f956cc03bd750ebc-3271128b70b8e57d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6ec-e364-796a-b544-183433e5f1dd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6ece74172df9c584a52539772f3"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T16:59:55.493Z"}
