+ contracts/golden/manifest.json with empty files [] in tmp (manifest schema allows empty array). Then registry check passes.\n\nBut manifest schema validate requires files array; empty ok. Then listRegisteredDirs empty → ok.\n\nAlso `*` single segment test and `**` cross-segment.\n\nNeed `git init` and commit with -c flags. Use spawnSync('git', ['-c','user.name=t',...]). Commit requires files staged.\n\n45: scope-from front matter: write markdown tmp with front matter write_scope list; same git repo; run with --scope-from → same result. Missing front matter → exit 2.\n\n46: real repo check-no-collab exit 0 (spawnSync on script).\n47: fixtures.\n\n48: renderContractDoc(repoRoot) === docs content normalized; no \\r, no BOM.\n49: tmp root: copy contracts + docs, modify docs/contract.md one char, run check-contract-doc --root tmp → stale, exit 1.\n   Need tmp to contain everything renderContractDoc needs: contracts/registry.snapshot.json, contracts/golden/manifest.json, contracts/schemas. Copy contracts dir and docs dir.\n50: embedded interfaces §5 lists compared to snapshot.\n51: check scripts discoverable: names exist matching ^check-.*\\.mjs$ incl four.\n\nThat's a lot of code but straightforward.\n\nNote: tests must use `test()` flat. Titles exact.\n\nAlso careful: test files must contain `[AC-xxx]` literal → yes in titles.\n\nCareful about run-tests discovery: test/contract/*.test.mjs are enumerated — good.\n\nAlso `findOrphans` excludes test/fixtures.\n\nLet me now write registry.test.mjs.\n\nFor test 4 embedded table, exit map object.\n\nOne more: test 2 requires `getCode` behavior? Add assertions.\n\nNow write.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6ece74172d