r' not a catalog value. ✓\n\nWord rules: 'claude-sonnet-5-5-extra' — needles include id 'claude-sonnet-5-5' → match with after '-'. ✓ Also 'agent-large'? no.\n\n'use claude here' → 'claude' matches with spaces. ✓\n'claudette' → 'claude' at 0, after 't' alnum → no. But also id... no. ✓\n'codexes' → 'codex' followed by 'e' → no. ✓\n\nNote catalog cli list includes 'agent' and 'codex'; injecting value 'agent' alone in test 30 e.g. {x:'agent'} → matches.\n\nCareful test 30 with value 'claude:claude-sonnet-5-5': contains 'claude' too → hits at same path for two needles (different match) — that's 2 hits at same path. My dedupe key is path+needle, so 2 hits. Test asserts some hit with path; fine. But assert `hits.length >= 1`.\n\nTest 33: build doc:\n```js\nconst call = {command:'node', args:['bin/cliworker.mjs','run','--lease','l_abc','--state-dir','/s','--config','/c'], cwd:'C:/work/zeta-model-9', input:'stdin', output:'cliworker.event/v1', timeout_ms:1000}\n```\ncatalog include zeta-model-9. Wait design test 33 says cwd contains claude-sonnet-5-5 → still 0 hits. Use that.\n\ndoc = {models:[{lease_id:'l_abc', call}], calls:[call]}.\n\nBad variants: {call: {...call, command:'claude'}} → expect 1 hit kind call_mismatch path /models/0/call/command and another for /calls/0/command. So total 2. Test asserts `hits.filter(kind==='call_mismatch').length === 2`? Design says \"各一个 call_mismatch\" per variant — probably per subtree. For single-call docs I'll test models only to keep counts precise, and separately test calls.\n\nLet me structure: use doc with only models for mutation tests (1 call) and separately a doc with only calls (top-level) to check.\n\nCareful: doc {calls:[call]} without models → lease unknown → requires args[3] match ^l_ → 'l_abc' ok. Then command change etc.\n\nActually rootModels === null when no models → `calls` not treated as call subtree! My scan requires rootModels !== null. Hmm, design: \"顶层数组 calls 的每个元素\" — regardless of models presence. But `<lease