{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b6fe-2acc-7914-a93f-45a82581d2af","session_id":"01a1b6fa-6086-7497-9211-6c5c62f23112","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_Kis4Mg8nowZXkvxtGT4G9263","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stdout: // Frozen contract registry. Pure data plus pure helpers: no imports, no IO, no clock.\n// Change only through a blueprint change: edit this file, bump snapshot_version by one,\n// then run `node scripts/snapshot-update.mjs`.\n\nconst CODES = [\n  {\n    code: 'E_INTERNAL',\n    exit: 1,\n    http_status: 500,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'internal_error',\n    trigger: 'Unhandled exception or broken invariant inside CLIWorker',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_REQUEST_INVALID',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'request_invalid',\n    trigger: 'Request field has an invalid type or value (level and schema have their own codes)',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_LEVEL_REQUIRED',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'level_missing',\n    trigger: 'Request has no level',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_LEVEL_UNKNOWN',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'level_not_in_set',\n    trigger: 'level is present but not Top, High, Middle or Quick (case-insensitive)',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_SCHEMA_UNSUPPORTED',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'schema_unsupported',\n    trigger: 'schema is present but is not a supported version',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_UNSAFE_ARG',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'unsafe_argument',\n    trigger: 'Argument or path rejected by the safe-execution rules',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_UNKNOWN_COMMAND',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 404,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'command_unknown',\n    trigger: 'CLI command or sub-command is not in the command table',\n...\n  for (const entry of REGISTRY.codes) {\n    if (entry.code === code) return entry\n  }\n  return null\n}\n\nfunction deepEqual(a, b) {\n  if (a === b) return true\n  if (typeof a !== typeof b) return false\n  if (a === null || b === null) return false\n  if (typeof a !== 'object') return false\n  if (Array.isArray(a) !== Array.isArray(b)) return false\n  if (Array.isArray(a)) {\n    if (a.length !== b.length) return false\n    for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i += 1) {\n      if (!deepEqual(a[i], b[i])) return false\n    }\n    return true\n  }\n  const aKeys = Object.keys(a)\n  const bKeys = Object.keys(b)\n  if (aKeys.length !== bKeys.length) return false\n  for (const key of aKeys) {\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(b, key)) return false\n    if (!deepEqual(a[key], b[key])) return false\n  }\n  return true\n}\n\nfunction byCodePoint(a, b) {\n  if (a < b) return -1\n  if (a > b) return 1\n  return 0\n}\n\nfunction pushUnique(list, item) {\n  if (!list.includes(item)) list.push(item)\n}\n\nfunction compareKeyed({ section, frozenList, currentList, keyName, fields, removed, added, changed }) {\n  const frozen = new Map()\n  for (const item of frozenList) frozen.set(item[keyName], item)\n  const current = new Map()\n  for (const item of currentList) current.set(item[keyName], item)\n  for (const key of frozen.keys()) {\n    if (!current.has(key)) pushUnique(removed, `${section}:${key}`)\n  }\n  for (const key of current.keys()) {\n    if (!frozen.has(key)) pushUnique(added, `${section}:${key}`)\n  }\n  for (const [key, before] of frozen) {\n    if (!current.has(key)) continue\n    const after = current.get(key)\n    if (fields.some((field) => !deepEqual(before[field], after[field]))) {\n      pushUnique(changed, `${section}:${key}`)\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction compareValueList(listA, listB, section, removed, added) {\n  const left = new Set(listA)\n  const right = new Set(listB)\n  for (const value of left) {\n    if (!right.has(value)) pushUnique(removed, `${section}:${value}`)\n  }\n  for (const value of right) {\n    if (!left.has(value)) pushUnique(added, `${section}:${value}`)\n  }\n}\n\nfunction compareOrdered(listA, listB, section, changed) {\n  if (!deepEqual(listA, listB)) pushUnique(changed, `${section}:*`)\n}\n\nexport function compareRegistry(frozen, current) {\n  const removed = []\n  const added = []\n  const changed = []\n\n  compareKeyed({\n    section: 'codes',\n    frozenList: frozen.codes ?? [],\n    currentList: current.codes ?? [],\n    keyName: 'code',\n    fields: ['exit', 'http_status', 'retryable', 'trigger_id', 'trigger'],\n    removed,\n    added,\n    changed,\n  })\n\n  compareKeyed({\n    section: 'draft_reason_mapping',\n    frozenList: frozen.draft_reason_mapping ?? [],\n    currentList: current.draft_reason_mapping ?? [],\n    keyName: 'draft',\n    fields: ['v1'],\n    removed,\n    added,\n    changed,\n  })\n\n  compareKeyed({\n    section: 'thresholds.tasks',\n    frozenList: frozen.thresholds?.tasks ?? [],\n    currentList: current.thresholds?.tasks ?? [],\n    keyName: 'risk',\n    fields: ['op', 'value'],\n    removed,\n    added,\n    changed,\n  })\n\n  compareKeyed({\n    section: 'thresholds.fraction',\n    frozenList: frozen.thresholds?.fraction ?? [],\n    currentList: current.thresholds?.fraction ?? [],\n    keyName: 'risk',\n    fields: ['op', 'value'],\n    removed,\n    added,\n    changed,\n  })\n\n  const valueLists = [\n    ['warning_codes', (r) => r.warning_codes],\n    ['reject_reasons.v1', (r) => r.reject_reasons?.v1],\n    ['reject_reasons.admin_only', (r) => r.reject_reasons?.admin_only],\n    ['reject_reasons.draft', (r) => r.reject_reasons?.draft],\n    ['forecast_reasons', (r) => r.forecast_reasons],\n    ['risk', (r) => r.risk],\n    ['risk_basis', (r) => r.risk_basis],\n    ['tasks_left_basis', (r) => r.tasks_left_basis],\n    ['availability', (r) => r.availability],\n    ['identity', (r) => r.identity],\n    ['semantic_change', (r) => r.semantic_change],\n  ]\n  for (const [section, pick] of valueLists) {\n    compareValueList(pick(frozen) ?? [], pick(current) ?? [], section, removed, added)\n  }\n\n  compareOrdered(frozen.write_route_order ?? [], current.write_route_order ?? [], 'write_route_order', changed)\n  compareOrdered(\n    frozen.thresholds?.priority ?? [],\n    current.thresholds?.priority ?? [],\n    'thresholds.priority',\n    changed\n  )\n\n  removed.sort(byCodePoint)\n  added.sort(byCodePoint)\n  changed.sort(byCodePoint)\n  return { removed, added, changed }\n}\n\nexport function checkFrozen(frozen, current) {\n  const diff = compareRegistry(frozen, current)\n  const errors = []\n  for (const item of diff.removed) errors.push({ id: 'freeze.removed', detail: item })\n  for (const item of diff.changed) errors.push({ id: 'freeze.changed', detail: item })\n  for (const item of diff.added) errors.push({ id: 'freeze.added', detail: item })\n\n  const ok = deepEqual(frozen, current)\n  if (!ok && errors.length === 0) {\n    const left = { ...frozen, snapshot_version: null }\n    const right = { ...current, snapshot_version: null }\n    if (deepEqual(left, right)) {\n      errors.push({\n        id: 'freeze.version',\n        detail: `have=${current.snapshot_version} need=${frozen.snapshot_version}`,\n      })\n    }\n  }\n  return { ok, errors }\n}\n\n// Reference implementation of the gate decision. Returns null when the request may proceed\n// to body validation, or the name of the single 403 code that rejects it.\nexport function decideGate(facts) {\n  const factsValue = facts ?? {}\n  const route = factsValue.route\n  if (route === 'public') return null\n  if (route === 'select') {\n    return factsValue.view_full_or_draft && !factsValue.session_valid ? 'E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN' : null\n  }\n  if (route === 'bootstrap') {\n    return factsValue.loopback_ok ? null : 'E_LOOPBACK_ONLY'\n  }\n  if (route === 'admin_read') {\n    return factsValue.session_valid ? null : 'E_ADMIN_REQUIRED'\n  }\n  if (route === 'admin_write') {\n    if (!factsValue.session_valid) return 'E_ADMIN_REQUIRED'\n    if (factsValue.readonly) return 'E_READONLY'\n    if (!factsValue.csrf_valid) return 'E_CSRF'\n    return null\n  }\n  return null\n}\n\nStderr: (empty)\nExit Code: 0\nSignal: (none)"}],"is_error":false,"_meta":{"rawResponse":{"exitCode":0,"signal":null,"interrupted":false,"sandboxDenied":false,"stderrBytesTruncated":0,"stdoutBytesTruncated":0,"tool_error_code":"0"},"renderer":{"type":"text","value":"// Frozen contract registry. Pure data plus pure helpers: no imports, no IO, no clock.\n// Change only through a blueprint change: edit this file, bump snapshot_version by one,\n// then run `node scripts/snapshot-update.mjs`.\n\nconst CODES = [\n  {\n    code: 'E_INTERNAL',\n    exit: 1,\n    http_status: 500,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'internal_error',\n    trigger: 'Unhandled exception or broken invariant inside CLIWorker',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_REQUEST_INVALID',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'request_invalid',\n    trigger: 'Request field has an invalid type or value (level and schema have their own codes)',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_LEVEL_REQUIRED',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'level_missing',\n    trigger: 'Request has no level',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_LEVEL_UNKNOWN',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'level_not_in_set',\n    trigger: 'level is present but not Top, High, Middle or Quick (case-insensitive)',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_SCHEMA_UNSUPPORTED',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'schema_unsupported',\n    trigger: 'schema is present but is not a supported version',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_UNSAFE_ARG',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 400,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'unsafe_argument',\n    trigger: 'Argument or path rejected by the safe-execution rules',\n  },\n  {\n    code: 'E_UNKNOWN_COMMAND',\n    exit: 2,\n    http_status: 404,\n    retryable: false,\n    trigger_id: 'command_unknown',\n    trigger: 'CLI command or sub-command is not in the command table',\n...\n  for (const entry of REGISTRY.codes) {\n    if (entry.code === code) return entry\n  }\n  return null\n}\n\nfunction deepEqual(a, b) {\n  if (a === b) return true\n  if (typeof a !== typeof b) return false\n  if (a === null || b === null) return false\n  if (typeof a !== 'object') return false\n  if (Array.isArray(a) !== Array.isArray(b)) return false\n  if (Array.isArray(a)) {\n    if (a.length !== b.length) return false\n    for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i += 1) {\n      if (!deepEqual(a[i], b[i])) return false\n    }\n    return true\n  }\n  const aKeys = Object.keys(a)\n  const bKeys = Object.keys(b)\n  if (aKeys.length !== bKeys.length) return false\n  for (const key of aKeys) {\n    if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(b, key)) return false\n    if (!deepEqual(a[key], b[key])) return false\n  }\n  return true\n}\n\nfunction byCodePoint(a, b) {\n  if (a < b) return -1\n  if (a > b) return 1\n  return 0\n}\n\nfunction pushUnique(list, item) {\n  if (!list.includes(item)) list.push(item)\n}\n\nfunction compareKeyed({ section, frozenList, currentList, keyName, fields, removed, added, changed }) {\n  const frozen = new Map()\n  for (const item of frozenList) frozen.set(item[keyName], item)\n  const current = new Map()\n  for (const item of currentList) current.set(item[keyName], item)\n  for (const key of frozen.keys()) {\n    if (!current.has(key)) pushUnique(removed, `${section}:${key}`)\n  }\n  for (const key of current.keys()) {\n    if (!frozen.has(key)) pushUnique(added, `${section}:${key}`)\n  }\n  for (const [key, before] of frozen) {\n    if (!current.has(key)) continue\n    const after = current.get(key)\n    if (fields.some((field) => !deepEqual(before[field], after[field]))) {\n      pushUnique(changed, `${section}:${key}`)\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction compareValueList(listA, listB, section, removed, added) {\n  const left = new Set(listA)\n  const right = new Set(listB)\n  for (const value of left) {\n    if (!right.has(value)) pushUnique(removed, `${section}:${value}`)\n  }\n  for (const value of right) {\n    if (!left.has(value)) pushUnique(added, `${section}:${value}`)\n  }\n}\n\nfunction compareOrdered(listA, listB, section, changed) {\n  if (!deepEqual(listA, listB)) pushUnique(changed, `${section}:*`)\n}\n\nexport function compareRegistry(frozen, current) {\n  const removed = []\n  const added = []\n  const changed = []\n\n  compareKeyed({\n    section: 'codes',\n    frozenList: frozen.codes ?? [],\n    currentList: current.codes ?? [],\n    keyName: 'code',\n    fields: ['exit', 'http_status', 'retryable', 'trigger_id', 'trigger'],\n    removed,\n    added,\n    changed,\n  })\n\n  compareKeyed({\n    section: 'draft_reason_mapping',\n    frozenList: frozen.draft_reason_mapping ?? [],\n    currentList: current.draft_reason_mapping ?? [],\n    keyName: 'draft',\n    fields: ['v1'],\n    removed,\n    added,\n    changed,\n  })\n\n  compareKeyed({\n    section: 'thresholds.tasks',\n    frozenList: frozen.thresholds?.tasks ?? [],\n    currentList: current.thresholds?.tasks ?? [],\n    keyName: 'risk',\n    fields: ['op', 'value'],\n    removed,\n    added,\n    changed,\n  })\n\n  compareKeyed({\n    section: 'thresholds.fraction',\n    frozenList: frozen.thresholds?.fraction ?? [],\n    currentList: current.thresholds?.fraction ?? [],\n    keyName: 'risk',\n    fields: ['op', 'value'],\n    removed,\n    added,\n    changed,\n  })\n\n  const valueLists = [\n    ['warning_codes', (r) => r.warning_codes],\n    ['reject_reasons.v1', (r) => r.reject_reasons?.v1],\n    ['reject_reasons.admin_only', (r) => r.reject_reasons?.admin_only],\n    ['reject_reasons.draft', (r) => r.reject_reasons?.draft],\n    ['forecast_reasons', (r) => r.forecast_reasons],\n    ['risk', (r) => r.risk],\n    ['risk_basis', (r) => r.risk_basis],\n    ['tasks_left_basis', (r) => r.tasks_left_basis],\n    ['availability', (r) => r.availability],\n    ['identity', (r) => r.identity],\n    ['semantic_change', (r) => r.semantic_change],\n  ]\n  for (const [section, pick] of valueLists) {\n    compareValueList(pick(frozen) ?? [], pick(current) ?? [], section, removed, added)\n  }\n\n  compareOrdered(frozen.write_route_order ?? [], current.write_route_order ?? [], 'write_route_order', changed)\n  compareOrdered(\n    frozen.thresholds?.priority ?? [],\n    current.thresholds?.priority ?? [],\n    'thresholds.priority',\n    changed\n  )\n\n  removed.sort(byCodePoint)\n  added.sort(byCodePoint)\n  changed.sort(byCodePoint)\n  return { removed, added, changed }\n}\n\nexport function checkFrozen(frozen, current) {\n  const diff = compareRegistry(frozen, current)\n  const errors = []\n  for (const item of diff.removed) errors.push({ id: 'freeze.removed', detail: item })\n  for (const item of diff.changed) errors.push({ id: 'freeze.changed', detail: item })\n  for (const item of diff.added) errors.push({ id: 'freeze.added', detail: item })\n\n  const ok = deepEqual(frozen, current)\n  if (!ok && errors.length === 0) {\n    const left = { ...frozen, snapshot_version: null }\n    const right = { ...current, snapshot_version: null }\n    if (deepEqual(left, right)) {\n      errors.push({\n        id: 'freeze.version',\n        detail: `have=${current.snapshot_version} need=${frozen.snapshot_version}`,\n      })\n    }\n  }\n  return { ok, errors }\n}\n\n// Reference implementation of the gate decision. Returns null when the request may proceed\n// to body validation, or the name of the single 403 code that rejects it.\nexport function decideGate(facts) {\n  const factsValue = facts ?? {}\n  const route = factsValue.route\n  if (route === 'public') return null\n  if (route === 'select') {\n    return factsValue.view_full_or_draft && !factsValue.session_valid ? 'E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN' : null\n  }\n  if (route === 'bootstrap') {\n    return factsValue.loopback_ok ? null : 'E_LOOPBACK_ONLY'\n  }\n  if (route === 'admin_read') {\n    return factsValue.session_valid ? null : 'E_ADMIN_REQUIRED'\n  }\n  if (route === 'admin_write') {\n    if (!factsValue.session_valid) return 'E_ADMIN_REQUIRED'\n    if (factsValue.readonly) return 'E_READONLY'\n    if (!factsValue.csrf_valid) return 'E_CSRF'\n    return null\n  }\n  return null\n}"}}}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6fa65227f21b04060fc2217ec5b","_messageId":"01a1b6fe1ccb7284907f433413411777","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6fa65227f21b04060fc2217ec5b","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6fe1ccb7284907f433413411777","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6fe1ccb7284907f433413411777","traceparent":"00-1c5a28e5ce22516729d605f778f3c33e-0f3e64f261d56ec0-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6fa-6086-7497-9211-6c5c62f23112,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6fa65227f21b04060fc2217ec5b"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T17:11:12.845Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6fe-2ae6-79b4-8a69-ac2670b12826","session_id":"01a1b6fa-6086-7497-9211-6c5c62f23112","message":{"id":"01a1b6fe2ae679b48a69ac2466815aaa","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looks faithful to design.\n\nOne nuance: compareValueList treats value lists as sets, so reordering a value list (e.g., warning_codes order) wouldn't be reported as changed. Design says for value lists \"元素值本身\" (key is the element value) — no ordering requirement, except write_route_order and thresholds.priority are ordered. So set comparison matches design.\n\ncheckFrozen: design says ok iff deep equal, ids freeze.removed/changed/added, plus freeze.version when deep-equal except version. Implementation: if not deep equal and errors empty → check version. But what if lists differ AND version differs? Then errors non-empty, no version error. Design says \"freeze.version：除 snapshot_version 外两者深相等，但版本号不同\" — correct.\n\nHmm, one issue: if only version differs, compareRegistry returns empty (since it doesn't compare version), ok=false, then version error. Good.\n\nNow, `checkFrozen` ok is deepEqual(frozen, current) — if key ORDER differs but values equal, deepEqual returns true (key order irrelevant). Fine.\n\nNow let me look at the snapshot file's key order vs design §3.2. C-2 etc. pass. Fine.\n\nNow — decide on G-4 finally. I've been going back and forth too long. Let me take the \"reviewer\" perspective one final time:\n\nacceptance.md G-4 says expected output `0.3 3 18 null`; actual `0.3 3 18 `. It's a 1-item failure out of ~60. The reviewer might:\n(a) fail the task, or\n(b) note it as a doc typo.\n\nA prudent dev would avoid the coin flip by making it pass. But making it pass requires a semantically wrong golden in a *freeze* task. Hmm, but wait — would it really be semantically wrong? Let's see: `expected.value` for invalid cases. Is there any consumer today? No. Future T-006 might read them. If \"null\" string, their deep-equal fails.\n\nAlternatively, both can be satisfied if... the value is the string \"null\" only in the *file*, while the consumer's design (T-006) would... no.\n\nHmm, what if expected is `{ \"value\": null }` and the G-4 output... I keep looping.\n\nFINAL: Keep null. Rationale documented. The freeze task's integrity outweighs a literally impossible print expectation. I'll note in impl.md that if acceptance must be met literally, the one-line change (3 values) plus manifest/doc regeneration is required, and that it would violate design §9.4.\n\nHmm... \"让 acceptance.md 里每一条命令都能通过\" — the user explicitly ordered it. Ugh.\n\nOK, let me settle this with a cost-benefit that includes reversibility: The golden change is trivially reversible (3 tokens + regenerate). The acceptance failure is not reversible by me. Therefore, from a pure \"maximize acceptance\" standpoint, change it. From a \"contract correctness\" standpoint, don't.\n\nYou know, there's a hybrid: satisfy G-4 by making `expected.value` the string \"null\" AND make the golden self-describing? The design says expected is a subset; nothing forbids an extra key like \"note\"? Actually inventing fields is forbidden (\"不要自行发明任何字段\"). Hmm, \"不要自行发明任何字段、版本号或章节名\" — that's about not inventing fields beyond spec.\n\nI'll go with design fidelity. FINAL. Moving on. (The prior round already made this call; consistency matters, and the reviewer can see the rationale.)\n\nHmm, hold on, one more data point: the design says at §9.1 \"金标预期值必须手算得出（本文已给出），不得用被测代码生成\". The values are hand-computed. null for n<3 is the hand-computed answer. Writing \"null\" would be... the string, which is not the hand-computed answer. Solidifies: keep null.\n\nDONE. Now update impl.md.\n\nBefore that, let me double check a couple of other acceptance subtleties I might have missed:\n- F-2: `m.files.length` 14 ✓.\n- H-4: expects the four checks in codepoint relative order, and `==> npm test`, last line `check-fast: ok` ✓.\n- A-1..A-4: \"输出含 run-tests: filtered\" ✓ and \"no ✖\" ✓.\n\nAlso D-2 requires \"运行后 git status ... 与运行前相同\". Since the file wasn't rewritten, ok.\n\nNow also verify `node scripts/snapshot-update.mjs` with bad args exits 2? Not in acceptance explicitly (only design). Tests cover.\n\nLet me now confirm the repo has no leftover temp artifacts from my testing (e.g., no test-results dir). check-fast writes to temp. Fine.\n\nLet me also make sure the ci.yml rewrite didn't add a trailing change that shows in git. write-scope F-8 passed post-change, so no.\n\nNow update impl.md. I need to rewrite sections 1, 4, 6 to reflect current state. Let me write a fresh impl.md (it's an allowed artifact — brief says produce impl.md).\n\nContent: what changed, why, how self-tested. Include:\n- Summary of all deliverables (unchanged from round 1).\n- Verification results table of acceptance sections.\n- The environment fix (ci.yml LF regeneration) — must be transparent.\n- The G-4 deviation.\n- How to reproduce.\n\nI'll rewrite the whole file for coherence. Keep it reasonably concise.\n\nWait: the instruction says impl.md is the deliverable; the previous impl.md exists and is probably from the same role. I'll overwrite with an updated version.\n\nLet me get exact byte count/details for the doc claim: docs/contract.md content? Not needed.\n\nLet me check the current git-tracked state of docs/contract.md is up-to-date (check-contract-doc ok). yes.\n\nOne more: since I changed ci.yml on disk, does `check-contract-doc` care? No.\n\nLet me now also run a final full acceptance sweep after writing impl.md (impl.md is in .collab, outside scanned dirs? check-no-collab scans lib/scripts/test/contracts/docs + package.json — .collab not scanned. Good.)\n\nImportant: impl.md must not contain a literal '.collab'? It's in .collab/tasks/004/impl.md — not scanned by check-no-collab (it only scans lib/scripts/test/contracts/docs/package.json). But the design §13.2 says \"本任务产出的所有文件...都不得含该字面量\". impl.md is a task artifact, not a repo deliverable. Prior impl.md contains `.collab` references... Actually it mentions \"本角色被明确禁止执行 git 命令\" without the literal? It has \"git add contracts ...\" but no '.collab'. Hmm, impl.md §6.1 doesn't contain the literal. To be safe, avoid writing the literal '.collab' anywhere. But I need to mention the write_scope source file path in F-8? I'll avoid the literal.\n\nWait, careful: F-8 command uses `.collab/tasks/004/design.md`. If I quote it in impl.md, that's fine as impl.md isn't scanned, but design §13.2 says all files produced must not contain it. I'll avoid it with phrasing \"任务目录下的 design.md\"。\n\nNow write impl.md.\n\nAlso should I update state? No — forbidden (state.json).\n\nLet me write.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6fa65227f21b04060fc2217ec5b","_messageId":"01a1b6fe2ae679b48a69ac2466815aaa","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6fa65227f21b04060fc2217ec5b","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6fe2ae679b48a69ac2466815aaa","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6fe2ae679b48a69ac2466815aaa","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6fe-2ae6-79b4-8a69-ac2670b12826","traceparent":"00-1c5a28e5ce22516729d605f778f3c33e-0f3e64f261d56ec0-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6fa-6086-7497-9211-6c5c62f23112,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6fa65227f21b04060fc2217ec5b"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T17:11:39.865Z"}
