nce command could be considered as \"expected output\" describing semantics. Since acceptance.md is the file I'm asked to rewrite into a parseable format, I could keep the command identical but adjust the expected assertion? No — I must not change substance.\n\nHmm. Actually, maybe I should reconsider: since acceptance.md must be rewritten, maybe the rewritten version can express expectations as bullet assertions (\"one of the printed values is null\"). The user note says: \"each check body a fenced block whose FIRST line is the runnable command, then bullet assertions\". So the format is: command first line, then bullet assertions. In the 001 example the expectations are prose lines after the code block, not bullets. But the note explicitly says \"followed by bullet assertions.\"\n\nLet me look at how the CI extracts commands — check scripts/check-ci.mjs? That's for ci matrix. Hmm, where's the acceptance runner? Maybe in .collab/harness or similar. Let me look for the parser that extracts commands from acceptance.md — grep for \"zero commands extracted\".\n\nLet me search the repo/.collab for relevant harness code.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6feff49796cac64907b9aede7fa","_messageId":"01a1b6ff5db474a3b148e0621329ce1f","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6feff49796cac64907b9aede7fa","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6ff5db474a3b148e0621329ce1f","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6ff5db474a3b148e0621329ce1f","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6ff-5db4-74a3-b148-e064f997e180","traceparent":"00-d07ca3abfc605747357a7a326176e150-8a1b5f038facd949-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6fe-fae8-7ef3-a121-2a6d3b88b5a9,codebuddy.conversation_reques