{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b6ff-9158-73c9-a545-08a15b58a563","session_id":"01a1b6fe-fae8-7ef3-a121-2a6d3b88b5a9","message":{"id":"01a1b6ff915873c9a545089fd0897bb4","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Not helpful. Let me instead check the CI runner's behavior: \"CI runner rejected acceptance.md: exit 2, zero commands extracted, ci-results.json not written.\" So the harness extracts commands from acceptance.md, presumably from fenced code blocks within `## ` sections. My acceptance.md uses tables with inline command cells → zero commands. Need reformat.\n\nSince I can't see the parser, follow the note literally:\n- one check per `## ` section\n- each check body a fenced block whose FIRST line is the runnable command\n- then bullet assertions\n- No tables, no `###` subsections.\n\n\"one check per '## ' section\" — in 001's format, there are `## 0` sections with `### X-01` subsections. But the note says no `###`. So each check must be a `## ` section. And sections like \"conventions\" preamble are fine (no commands)?\n\nHmm, but if every `## ` section is a check, then a preamble `## 约定` section would be parsed as a check with no fenced command. Risky. Better: make every `## ` section a check containing exactly one fenced block with the command(s) first line + assertions. Put conventions before the first `## ` (in the H1 preamble area) or as `# 约定`? The instructions: \"one check per '## ' section, each check body a fenced block whose FIRST line is the runnable command, then bullet assertions.\"\n\nAlso note \"each check is a '## ' section whose body starts with a triple-backtick fence containing ONE runnable command line\". So ONE command per block. That conflicts with F-3 etc. which need multiple PowerShell lines (setup + run). Hmm — \"contains ONE runnable command line\". Perhaps commands should be single-line each; multi-statement must be a single line? In PowerShell, `;` separates statements. Long single lines are ugly but acceptable.\n\nAlternatively, allow the fenced block to contain a command (which may be a multi-line powershell script)? The note says ONE runnable command line. Safest: make each check's fenced block exactly one line. For scenarios needing temp dirs + modification + run, I can write a single-line PowerShell command chain. That's doable but long. Alternatively use `node -e \"...\"` one-liners that do everything (copy, modify, spawn check script, print). That's cleaner and exactly one line.\n\nBut careful: node -e with a script that spawns the check script — fine.\n\nSince the runner presumably executes each command and then asserts via its own judge or by running the assertions? Unclear. I'll write: `## <ID> <title>` then fenced block with one line, then bullets stating expected exit code and output.\n\nAlso exit code check: in pwsh, `\"exit=$LASTEXITCODE\"` at end of a single line works with `;`.\n\nNow, the big question: do I also need to keep the substance identical so the tests still pass? Yes.\n\nLet me now verify the implementation actually passes everything currently, then rewrite acceptance.md, then update impl.md.\n\nNote: I must not run git. But F-16 needs `git ls-files` to include the files. I can't stage. Hmm. But maybe previous dev staged them already (impl.md §6.1 says \"当前 33 个要求路径全部已登记\"). Staging persists in the index, which is per-worktree... worktree has own index. Since the same worktree, index persists. So probably fine.\n\nBut careful: if I rewrite acceptance.md, that's an untracked/modified file in .collab — allowed via `--scope .collab/tasks/004/**`.\n\nLet me first verify current state by running the checks (non-git ones).\n\nPlan:\n1. Run the main checks to see the current pass/fail status.\n2. Rewrite acceptance.md to parseable format.\n3. Verify all commands (except git ones) pass; check git status indirectly? I can't run git... but F-8/F-9 are git-dependent and I can't verify. Hmm, \"禁止执行 git 命令\" — but `check-write-scope.mjs --base` internally runs git; running the script itself is not \"executing git commands\" directly... but it effectively does. I'd say running the acceptance scripts is required (\"让 acceptance.md 里每一条命令都能通过\"). The ban presumably means: don't commit/branch/checkout. Running `node scripts/check-write-scope.mjs --base ...` is an acceptance command, so it's fine.\n\nHmm, but `git add` is needed for F-16... I'll avoid. Previous dev already staged. I'll check by running F-16 command (it's a node command, invoking git internally...). Let's see. Actually F-16 uses execFileSync('git'). Running the acceptance command is legitimate. OK.\n\nLet me start verifying.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b6feff49796cac64907b9aede7fa","_messageId":"01a1b6ff915873c9a545089fd0897bb4","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b6feff49796cac64907b9aede7fa","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b6ff915873c9a545089fd0897bb4","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b6ff915873c9a545089fd0897bb4","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b6ff-9158-73c9-a545-08a15b58a563","traceparent":"00-d07ca3abfc605747357a7a326176e150-8a1b5f038facd949-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b6fe-fae8-7ef3-a121-2a6d3b88b5a9,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b6feff49796cac64907b9aede7fa"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T17:12:53.452Z"}
